# Every text file is stored with LF, and checked out with LF on every platform.
#
# The development machines are Windows. Without this file an editor that saves CRLF
# turns a three-line change into a whole-file rewrite, and the next merge reports a
# 3,000-line conflict that is really whitespace (trip-editor.tsx, PR #168). Pinning
# eol=lf keeps the working tree identical to the repository on Windows too, so the
# same file cannot flip its line endings on the way in.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary formats the repository holds now or is likely to gain. Marking them keeps
# git from ever trying to normalise or diff them as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.dump binary
